# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD is
# PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * the LLMNR / NBT-NS weakness lives in registry/adapter policy (no
#     dedicated foreground service to run);
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the vulnerable name-resolution policy is ALREADY
# in effect, so a fix sets the DisableMulticast / NetBIOS-over-TCP policy; no
# process runs as PID 1 that a restart could kill.
